  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/eYATWnakr-kiQU5ty-yDqhjJxpu06zyQ253A1841j0Y.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\nAs shown in the figure, a single conducting wire is bent to form a loop in the form of a circle of radius 'r' concentrically inside a square of side ' $a$ ', where $a: r=8: \\pi$. A battery B drives a current through the wire. If the battery B and the gap G are of negligible sizes, determine the strength of magnetic field at the common centre $O$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DUBbu",
      "text": "$\\cdot \\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mid}{2 \\pi a} \\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zWL1Y",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_{0} I}{2 \\pi a}(\\sqrt{2}+1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eBLqB",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_{0} I}{\\pi a} 2 \\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2}+1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Gh13j",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_{0} I}{\\pi \\mathrm{a}} 2 \\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$\\frac{a}{r}=\\frac{8}{\\pi}, r=\\frac{\\pi a}{8}$\r\n$B=\\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mid}{2 r}-\\frac{4 \\mu_{0} I}{4 \\pi a / 2} \\times \\sqrt{2}=\\frac{\\mu_{0} I}{2 r}-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\mu_{0} I}{\\pi a}=\\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mid \\times 8}{2 \\pi a}-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\mu_{0} I}{\\pi a}$\r\n$=\\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mid}{\\pi a}(4-2 \\sqrt{2})=\\frac{\\mu_{0} I}{\\pi a} 2 \\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1)$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/6sZgeMv7PyO9Y2zg3WIF_qA2-MAilswkDN4W6eSKAHc.original.fullsize.png\">",
